"1: # Production Planning Model — Version 2 (Mathematical Formulation)\n2: \n3: **Status:** v2 — formal LP formulation derived from `model_v1.md` (purpose, data, and decision semantics unchanged)\n4: **Date:** 2026-10-17\n5: **Model type:** Linear program (LP), continuous variables, single week\n6: \n7: ---\n8: \n9: ## 1. Decision Variables\n10: \n11: | Variable | Meaning | Units |\n12: |----------|---------|-------|\n13: | xA | Number of units of product A produced per week | units/week |\n14: | xB | Number of units of product B produced per week | units/week |\n15: \n16: Domain: xA ≥ 0, xB ≥ 0 (production quantities cannot be negative).\n17: Per v1's divisibility assumption, xA and xB are continuous (fractional units allowed).\n18: \n19: ## 2. Objective Function\n20: \n21: Maximize total weekly profit:\n22: \n23:     maximize  Z = 40·xA + 50·xB        [USD/week]\n24: \n25: Unit check: 40 USD/unit × xA units/week + 50 USD/unit × xB units/week → USD/week. ✔\n26: \n27: ## 3. Constraints\n28: \n29: ### 3.1 Machine-time capacity\n30: \n31: Total machine hours consumed per week must not exceed available capacity:\n32: \n33:     2·xA + 1·xB ≤ 100        [hours/week]\n34: \n35: Unit check: 2 h/unit × xA units/week + 1 h/unit × xB units/week = h/week ≤ 100 h/week. ✔\n36: \n37: ### 3.2 Labor capacity\n38: \n39: Total labor hours consumed per week must not exceed available capacity:\n40: \n41:     1·xA + 3·xB ≤ 90         [hours/week]\n42: \n43: Unit check: 1 h/unit × xA units/week + 3 h/unit × xB units/week = h/week ≤ 90 h/week. ✔\n44: \n45: ### 3.3 Nonnegativity\n46: \n47:     xA ≥ 0,  xB ≥ 0          [units/week]\n48: \n49: ## 4. Complete Model (compact form)\n50: \n51:     maximize    Z = 40·xA + 50·xB          [USD/week]\n52: \n53:     subject to  2·xA + 1·xB ≤ 100          [machine hours/week]\n54:                 1·xA + 3·xB ≤ 90           [labor hours/week]\n55:                 xA, xB ≥ 0                 [units/week]\n56: \n57: ## 5. Standard (Matrix) Form\n58: \n59: Equivalent formulation for simplex-style solution methods:\n60: \n61:     maximize    cᵀx\n62:     subject to  Ax ≤ b,  x ≥ 0\n63: \n64: with\n65: \n66:     x = [xA, xB]ᵀ              [units/week]\n67:     c = [40, 50]ᵀ              [USD/unit]\n68:     A = [ 2   1 ]              [hours/unit]\n69:         [ 1   3 ]\n70:     b = [100, 90]ᵀ             [hours/week]\n71: \n72: ## 6. Traceability to v1\n73: \n74: | v1 element (words)                    | v2 formalization        |\n75: |---------------------------------------|-------------------------|\n76: | Units of A/B produced per week        | xA, xB (units/week)     |\n77: | Weekly profit objective               | max 40·xA + 50·xB       |\n78: | Machine capacity limit (100 h)        | 2·xA + 1·xB ≤ 100       |\n79: | Labor capacity limit (90 h)           | 1·xA + 3·xB ≤ 90        |\n80: | No negative production                | xA, xB ≥ 0              |\n81: \n82: All coefficients are constants (deterministic, per v1 assumptions). No integrality, demand, or inventory constraints — those remain out of scope as in v1.\n[82 lines total]"